From d0ffeea2d04d7c212b901cd4c1d43bab62df5e49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:57:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Step the bitrate down on reported queueing delay

A patched client reports its queueing delay every 250 ms (FTDL). Two
reports in a row at or over frogtale_delay_ms (default 30) outside
handoff windows step down 15%, or 40% at 4x the threshold, at most once
a second. Climbing now also needs the queue under half the threshold,
so it stops where the link starts queueing instead of where it drops.
Like GeForce Now, this backs off before the queue overflows into loss.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MoWnCbHthvS5ddBE52YXAc
